-- title:
--   Mumford embedding from Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`.
--
--   **Numerical data.** A nonzero squarefree natural number $N$ (`hN`), primes $q,q'$ with $q\nmid N$ (`hqN`), $q'\nmid N$ (`hq'N`), $q'\neq q$ (`hqq'`), both at least $5$ (`hq5`, `hq'5`), and a nonzero $D$ divisible by $2Nqq'$ (`hD`). A valuation subring $A_2$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $A_2$ (`hA₂`, the predicate [`ValuationSubring.LiesOverPrime`](def/FLTPrelim_Ramification.html#L16)), and a height-one prime $v_2$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ containing $q$ (`hv₂`).
--
--   **Definite quaternion data at level $N$.** Rationals $a_1,b_1$ with $a_1<0$, $b_1<0$ such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ is a division algebra exactly at the place $v$ containing $q'$ (`hdef₁`); a maximal order $\Lambda_1$ (an order maximal among the orders containing it, `hΛ₁`); an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$, i.e. an intersection of two maximal orders with relative index $N$ in the first (`hR₁`), contained in $\Lambda_1$ (`hRΛ₁`); a finite-idele unit $n_1$ in `primeHeckeSet R₁ q`, i.e. $n_1$ lies in the finite-adelic box of $R_1$, $q\,n_1^{-1}$ lies in that box, while $n_1^{-1}$ and $q^{-1}n_1$ do not (`hn₁`). The order $\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R_1\,n_1 = R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ is Eichler of level $Nq$ (`hS₁`) and is fixed by conjugation by $n_1$ (`hnorm₁`); the shift by $n_1$ on the class set of the finite-idele stabiliser of $\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R_1\,n_1$ is an involution (`hsq₁`); the two relevant class sets are finite; and `hlaws₁` asserts `ClassSetHeckeLaws N q Λ₁ R₁ n₁`, namely that the edge Hecke matrices commute pairwise, the vertex Hecke matrices commute pairwise, the two degeneracy pushforwards intertwine edge and vertex Hecke operators at primes other than $q$, and the joint kernel of the degeneracy maps is stable under the edge Hecke operators.
--
--   **Indefinite quaternion data.** Rationals $a,b$ with $0<a$ or $0<b$ such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ is a division algebra exactly at the places containing $q$ and $q'$ (`hB`), together with a maximal order $\Lambda$ (`hΛ`).
--
--   **Moduli data over $\mathbb Z[1/D]$ and the tower.** A field $\mathit{Fbar}$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ which is a curve over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (principal divisors of degree zero exist, residue fields at places are finite over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and $\Omega_{\mathit{Fbar}/\overline{\mathbb Q}}$ is free of rank one) and essentially of finite type; a scheme $X$ with a morphism $\pi_X$ to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of `Localization.Away ((D : ℕ) : ℤ)`, a $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-point $\overline s$ of that base, and a rule `pt` assigning to every fake elliptic curve with $\Lambda$-action and $N$-level structure over a commutative ring $S$ (the structure `FakeEllipticCurve Λ N S`) a point of $X$ over the given base morphism. The hypotheses `pt_iso`, `pt_pullback`, `pt_surjective`, `pt_injective` are the four coarse-moduli axioms for `pt` (invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with base change along ring maps and pullback of curves, and bijectivity on geometric points up to isomorphism over algebraically closed fields); the universal property is not assumed here. Further, a curve model $\mathfrak M$ of $\mathit{Fbar}$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, an isomorphism $e_{\mathfrak M}$ from $\mathfrak M.C$ to the pullback of $\pi_X$ along $\overline s$ whose composite with the second projection is the structure morphism of $\mathfrak M$ (`he𝔐`), a homomorphism $\mathrm{gal}$ from $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-automorphisms over $\mathbb Q$ to semilinear automorphisms of $\mathit{Fbar}$, tower data $\mathbb T$ of fields $\mathbb T.F(\ell)$ for primes $\ell\notin\{q,q'\}$ with two $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-embeddings $\mathbb T.\varphi(\ell,0)$, $\mathbb T.\varphi(\ell,1)$ of $\mathit{Fbar}$ into each, the corresponding Galois actions $\mathrm{galT}$, two semilinear automorphisms $W$ of $\mathit{Fbar}$ and $WT$ of each $\mathbb T.F(\ell)$, and a witness `tw : ModuliTowerWitnessD …` tying these objects to the moduli interpretation.
--
--   **Local data at $A_2$.** It is assumed (as a `Fact`) that the decomposition subgroup of $A_2$ over $\mathbb Q$ acts isometrically for the valuation of $A_2$. An injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map $\iota_2$ from $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ into $2\times 2$ matrices over [`ValuationSubring.ratClosure A₂`](def/ValuationSubring_CompletionRatClosure.html#L13) (the topological closure of the prime subfield in the completion of $A_2$) (`hι₂`), and a homomorphism $\rho_2$ to $\mathrm{PGL}_2$ of that ring which is the projectivisation of $\iota_2$ (`hρ₂`); a pseudo-uniformiser $\varpi_2$ for that ring inside the completion whose image is $q$ (`hϖ₂`), the ring `Omega.HolRingOf ϖ₂ ρ₂` of functions on the upper half-plane holomorphic on every affinoid being assumed a domain.
--
--   **Hecke elements and groups.** Elements $s_2(\ell)\in\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]^\times$ and finite ideles $sf_2(\ell)$ for each prime $\ell\notin\{q,q'\}$ such that (`hs₂`, four clauses) $sf_2(\ell)$ has component $s_2(\ell)$ at every place not containing $q$, component $1$ at the places containing $q$, the product of the diagonal finite idele of the scalar $\ell$ with $sf_2(\ell)^{-1}$ lies in `levelHeckeUSet Λ₁ (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` when $\ell\mid N$ and in `primeHeckeSet (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` otherwise, and the reduced norm of $s_2(\ell)$ is $\ell$. Subgroups $\Gamma_2$ indexed by `Option` of those primes, with $\Gamma_2(\mathrm{none})$ the set of units lying in `CosetGraph.awayUnits R₁ v₂` (integral at every place other than $v_2$ for $R_1$) whose reduced norm has even $q$-adic valuation (`hΓ₂0`), and $\Gamma_2(\mathrm{some}\,\ell)=\Gamma_2(\mathrm{none})\cap s_2(\ell)\Gamma_2(\mathrm{none})s_2(\ell)^{-1}$ (`hΓ₂ℓ`). Elements $w_2$, $\overline w_2$ indexed likewise: `hw₂` says $w_2(\mathrm{none})$ lies in `awayUnits R₁ v₂` with reduced norm $q$, and $w_2(\mathrm{some}\,\ell)$ lies in `awayUnits (meetOrder R₁ (sf₂ ℓ)) v₂` with reduced norm $q$; `hwbar₂` says $\overline w_2(\mathrm{none})$ has reduced norm $q'$, is a unit of the local box of $R_1$ at every place $u\neq v_2$ not containing $q'$, and conjugation by it preserves the local boxes of $R_1$ and of $\Lambda_1$ at every $u\neq v_2$, and likewise for $\overline w_2(\mathrm{some}\,\ell)$ with $R_1$ replaced by $\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R_1\,(sf_2(\ell))$.
--
--   **Galois and parity data.** A homomorphism $d\mathrm{Iso}_2$ from the decomposition subgroup of $A_2$ over $\mathbb Q$ to isometric automorphisms of the completion whose underlying ring equivalence is the Galois action (`hdIso₂`); a character $\chi$ of the decomposition subgroup with values in $\mathbb Z/2$ which is trivial on inertia (`hχ₁`), nontrivial on any Frobenius at $q$ (`hχ₂`), and trivial exactly on the automorphisms fixing all elements of the residue field of $A_2$ satisfying $x^{q^2}=x$ (`hχ₃`).
--
--   **The $q$-adic base rings.** A characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O_0$ which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr₀`) with irreducible element $\pi$ (`hπ`), $\pi$-adically complete (`hcpl`), residue cardinality $q$ (`hres`) and absolutely unramified in the sense $(q)=(\pi)$ (`hunr`), with `ratClosure A₂` as its fraction field; an $\mathcal O_0$-algebra $Onr$, a characteristic-zero domain, with an $\mathcal O_0$-automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, complete for $(\pi)$ (`hOc`), with $(\pi)$ maximal (`hOm`), every element integral modulo $\pi$ (`hOa`), every monic polynomial of positive degree having a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOcl`), and $\mathrm{Fr}(x)\equiv x^q \pmod \pi$ (`hFr`); a determinant-valuation homomorphism $v\!\det$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of `ratClosure A₂` characterised by `hvdet`; a ring map $\psi_0$ from $Onr$ to the completion; the identifications $\pi\mapsto\varpi_2$ (`hπϖ`), invertibility of $N$ in $\mathcal O_0$ (`hN₀`), the description of the image of $\mathcal O_0$ as the unit ball (`h𝒪₀`), $\psi_0$ landing in the unit ball (`hψ₀`), compatibility of $\psi_0$ with $\mathcal O_0$ (`hψ₀𝒪`), and a rank-one condition on the valuation (`hrk`).
--
--   **Integral coarse moduli and correspondences.** An integral scheme $\mathcal X_0$ with a flat, separated, locally of finite type, quasi-compact morphism $f_0$ to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O_0$ and a point map $\mathrm{pt}_0$ making it a coarse moduli space for fake elliptic curves of level $N$ (`h𝒳₀`, including the universal property); schemes $\mathcal Y_0(\ell)$ with morphisms $g_0(\ell)$ and point maps $\mathrm{ptT}_0(\ell)$ which are coarse moduli spaces for such curves with extra $\ell$-level structure (`h𝒴₀`); two degeneracy morphisms $d_{0}(\ell),d_{1}(\ell)$ over the base (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`) realising on points the forgetting of the extra level (`hd₀`) and passage along an $\ell$-isogeny (`hd₁`); endomorphisms $\mathrm{ar}$, $\overline{\mathrm{ar}}$ of $\mathcal X_0$ over the base (`harf`, `harbarf`) realising on points the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $q$ (`har`) and at $q'$ (`harbar`).
--
--   **The formal uniformisation.** Natural families $\Theta$ and $\Theta_T(\ell)$ sending, for every $\mathcal O_0$-algebra $B$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, a pair consisting of an $\mathcal O_0$-algebra map $Onr\to B$ and a Deligne datum in `FormalOmega.Omega` to a $B$-point of $f_0$, resp. of $g_0(\ell)$. The hypothesis `hCD` (twelve clauses, summarised here) requires: naturality of $\Theta$ and of each $\Theta_T(\ell)$ in $B$; invariance of $\Theta$ under the twisted action `FormalOmega.OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` of the image under $\iota_2$ of elements of `awayUnits R₁ v₂`, and of $\Theta_T(\ell)$ under that of elements of `awayUnits R₁ v₂` intersected with its conjugate by $s_2(\ell)$; over every algebraically closed field $k$ with $\pi$ nilpotent and every fixed $\psi:Onr\to k$, surjectivity of $\Theta(\psi,\cdot)$ onto the $k$-points and the statement that two Deligne data have the same image exactly when they are related by the twisted action of such an element, and the same for each $\Theta_T(\ell)$; the universal property of $\Theta$, resp. each $\Theta_T(\ell)$, as a formal categorical quotient (every natural, twisted-invariant family into the nilpotent points of another scheme over $\mathcal O_0$ factors uniquely through it); compatibility of $\Theta_T(\ell)$ with $d_0(\ell)$ and, after a twist by $s_2(\ell)$, with $d_1(\ell)$; and compatibility of $\Theta$ with $\mathrm{ar}$ via the Frobenius twist of the $Onr$-component by $\mathrm{Fr}$, and with $\overline{\mathrm{ar}}$ via the twisted action of $\overline w_2(\mathrm{none})$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exists a ring homomorphism $\iota_0$ from $\mathit{Fbar}$ to the fraction field of `Omega.HolRingOf ϖ₂ ρ₂` such that:
--
--   1. on constants $\iota_0$ is the canonical map: for every $z\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $\iota_0$ of the image of $z$ in $\mathit{Fbar}$ equals the image of $z$ under the completion of $A_2$ followed by the structure map into that fraction field;
--
--   2. the subfield generated by the image of the completion of $A_2$ together with the image of $\iota_0$ equals `Mumford.invariantFieldOf` for the completion, the unit group $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]^\times$, the ring `Omega.HolRingOf ϖ₂ ρ₂` and the subgroup $\Gamma_2(\mathrm{none})$, i.e. the field of $\Gamma_2(\mathrm{none})$-invariants in that fraction field;
--
--   3. $\iota_0$ preserves linear independence: for every finite subset $t$ of $\mathit{Fbar}$ whose elements are linearly independent over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, the family of their images under $\iota_0$ is linearly independent over the completion of $A_2$;
--
--   4. $\iota_0$ is Galois-equivariant up to the parity twist: for every $\tau$ in the decomposition subgroup of $A_2$ over $\mathbb Q$ and every $x\in\mathit{Fbar}$, $\iota_0$ of the action of $\mathrm{gal}(\tau)$ on $x$ equals the action of $1$ if $\chi(\tau)=1$ and of $w_2(\mathrm{none})$ otherwise, applied to the image of $\iota_0(x)$ under the automorphism of the fraction field induced by the ambient semilinear automorphism attached to $d\mathrm{Iso}_2(\tau)$;
--
--   5. $\iota_0(W_0\cdot x)=w_2(\mathrm{none})\cdot\iota_0(x)$ for all $x\in\mathit{Fbar}$;
--
--   6. $\iota_0(W_1\cdot x)=\overline w_2(\mathrm{none})\cdot\iota_0(x)$ for all $x\in\mathit{Fbar}$;
--
--   7. for every prime $\ell\notin\{q,q'\}$ there is a ring homomorphism $\iota_\ell$ from $\mathbb T.F(\ell)$ to the same fraction field with $\iota_\ell\circ\mathbb T.\varphi(\ell,0)=\iota_0$ and $\iota_\ell(\mathbb T.\varphi(\ell,1)(x))=s_2(\ell)\cdot\iota_0(x)$ for all $x\in\mathit{Fbar}$.
--
--   This is the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation step in the form needed for the Shimura-curve tower: the function field of the geometric Shimura curve, and of each curve with auxiliary $\ell$-level structure, is embedded into the fraction field of the ring of rigid-analytic functions on Drinfeld's upper half-plane over the completion at $A_2$, the embedding being compatible with constants, with the $\Gamma_2$-invariants, with the decomposition group at $q$ up to the parity character $\chi$, with the two Atkin–Lehner involutions, and with the degeneracy maps of the tower. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_descentIntertwiningBase_of_moduliTowerWitness_zero_one_of_two_mul_dvd`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_descentIntertwiningBase_of_moduliTowerWitness_zero_one_of_two_mul_dvd), which assembles from it the intertwining base data for the descent to the rational Shimura curve.
